@page "/availabilityandmovementoffixedassets"
@inject AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets
@inject AfsModel AfsModel
<SeoHead Title="Fixed Assets Availability & Movement | UFIN"
         Description="Track availability, additions, disposals and depreciation of fixed assets across two reporting years for Ukrainian businesses." />

<RadzenCard Style="width: 100%;">
    <h2 class="text-center">@tableName</h2>
    <h5 class="text-end">(@ResLoc["thousandUAH"])</h5>
    <table class="table table-bordered py-0 table-sm table-striped">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <ThComponent Rowspan=2>@ResLoc["Period"]</ThComponent>
                <ThComponent Rowspan=2>@ResLoc["BalanceAtBeginOfYearAtOriginalCost"]</ThComponent>
                <ThComponent Colspan=2>@ResLoc["ReceivedForReportingPeriod"]</ThComponent>
                <ThComponent Colspan=2>@ResLoc["WithdrewInReportingPeriod"]</ThComponent>
                <ThComponent Rowspan=2>@ResLoc["BalanceAtEndOfYearAtOriginalBalanceAtEndOfYearAtOriginalCost"]</ThComponent>
                <ThComponent Rowspan=2>@ResLoc["BalanceAtEndOfYearMinusDepreciation"]</ThComponent>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <ThComponent>@ResLoc["total_"]</ThComponent>
                <ThComponent>@ResLoc["includingNew"]</ThComponent>
                <ThComponent>@ResLoc["total_"]</ThComponent>
                <ThComponent>@ResLoc["includingEliminated"]</ThComponent>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <TrAvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssetsComponent Item=@AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base>
                @MainModel.BaseYear&nbsp;@ResLoc["year"]
            </TrAvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssetsComponent>
            <TrAvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssetsComponent Item=@AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current>
                @MainModel.CurrentYear&nbsp;@ResLoc["year"]
            </TrAvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssetsComponent>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</RadzenCard>

<AIAnalysisPanel PromptBuilder="@BuildFixedAssetsAnalysisPrompt"
                 AnalyzeButtonLabel="@ResLoc["AnalyzeFixedAssetsMovement"]"
                 LoadingMessage="AI is analyzing fixed assets movement..." />

@code {
    // Set when the component is disposed. Checked inside the AI streaming callback to
    // prevent StateHasChanged() from being invoked on a disposed component (e.g. if the
    // user navigates away mid-analysis) and to release captured references for GC faster.
        private string? tableName;
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        string name = ResLoc["AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets"];
        int number = 5;

        tableName = String.Format("{0} {1}. {2} {3} {4}-{5} {6}", ResLoc["Table"], number, name, MainModel.CompanyName, MainModel.BaseYear, MainModel.CurrentYear, ResLoc["years"]);
        
        // Check AI availability on page load
        await base.OnInitializedAsync();
    }

                private string BuildFixedAssetsAnalysisPrompt()
    {
        string languageInstruction = AfsConstraints.GetLanguageInstruction();

        // Build structured data with proper column structure matching table
        var structuredData = $@"TABLE 5: AVAILABILITY AND MOVEMENT OF FIXED ASSETS
Company: {MainModel.CompanyName}
Period: {MainModel.BaseYear}-{MainModel.CurrentYear}
Unit: thousand UAH

COLUMN-BY-COLUMN DATA STRUCTURE:

**{MainModel.BaseYear} YEAR:**
   Beginning-of-year balance at historical cost: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtBeginInitialCost:N2}
   
   Received during the reporting period:
     - Total: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received:N2}
     - Including new: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.ReceivedNewlyAcquired:N2}
     - New as % of total received: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.ReceivedNewlyAcquired / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received * 100 : 0):N2}%
   
   Left in the reporting period:
     - Total: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left:N2}
     - Including liquidated: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Liquidated:N2}
     - Liquidated as % of total left: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Liquidated / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left * 100 : 0):N2}%
   
   End-of-year balance at historical cost: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost:N2}
   End-of-year balance net of depreciation: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation:N2}
   
   CALCULATED METRICS:
   Net change in year: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtBeginInitialCost:N2}
   Net addition (Received - Left): {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left:N2}
   Accumulated depreciation: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation:N2}
   Depreciation rate: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost > 0 ? (AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation) / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost * 100 : 0):N2}%
   Investment ratio (Received/Left): {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left : 0):N2}x

**{MainModel.CurrentYear} YEAR:**
   Beginning-of-year balance at historical cost: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtBeginInitialCost:N2}
   
   Received during the reporting period:
     - Total: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received:N2}
     - Including new: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.ReceivedNewlyAcquired:N2}
     - New as % of total received: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.ReceivedNewlyAcquired / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received * 100 : 0):N2}%
   
   Left in the reporting period:
     - Total: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left:N2}
     - Including liquidated: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Liquidated:N2}
     - Liquidated as % of total left: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Liquidated / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left * 100 : 0):N2}%
   
   End-of-year balance at historical cost: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost:N2}
   End-of-year balance net of depreciation: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation:N2}
   
   CALCULATED METRICS:
   Net change in year: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtBeginInitialCost:N2}
   Net addition (Received - Left): {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left:N2}
   Accumulated depreciation: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation:N2}
   Depreciation rate: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost > 0 ? (AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation) / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost * 100 : 0):N2}%
   Investment ratio (Received/Left): {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left : 0):N2}x

YEAR-OVER-YEAR COMPARISON:
   Change in capital investment: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received:N2} ({(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received > 0 ? (AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received) / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received * 100 : 0):N2}%)
   Change in disposals: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left:N2}
   Change in net book value: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation:N2}
";

        return $@"You are a financial analyst specializing in fixed assets management and capital investment analysis. Analyze the Availability and Movement of Fixed Assets for {MainModel.CompanyName}.

IMPORTANT: Respond in {languageInstruction} language. The user interface is in {languageInstruction}, so your entire response must be in {languageInstruction}.

{structuredData}

UNDERSTANDING THIS TABLE:
This table tracks the LIFECYCLE of fixed assets showing acquisitions, disposals, and depreciation.

**KEY CONCEPTS**:
1. **Historical Cost**: Original purchase price (doesn't change with age)
2. **Net of Depreciation**: Book value after accounting for wear and tear
3. **Received**: Assets acquired during the year
4. **New**: Brand new assets (vs used/transferred)
5. **Left**: Assets disposed/removed
6. **Liquidated**: Assets scrapped/written off (vs sold)

**ACCOUNTING EQUATION**:
Ending Balance = Beginning Balance + Received - Left

**CRITICAL QUALITY INDICATORS**:
â€¢ % New (of Received): 100% = all acquisitions are brand new (best)
â€¢ % Liquidated (of Left): 100% = all disposals were worthless (concerning)
â€¢ Depreciation Rate: Higher % = older assets, more worn
â€¢ Investment Ratio: Received/Left > 1 = expanding

CRITICAL FORMATTING RULES:
- DO NOT create or display any tables
- DO NOT repeat the raw data I provided
- The user can see all data in the table
- Focus ONLY on INTERPRETATION, INSIGHTS, and RECOMMENDATIONS
- Use narrative prose with clear sections and bullet points
- Reference numbers naturally in sentences

RESPONSE STRUCTURE:

**1. Executive Summary** (2-3 sentences)
- Capital investment strategy: Expansion, renewal, or contraction?
- Most significant finding
- Quick verdict

**2. Asset Base Trend**
- Beginning vs Ending balance for each year
- Net change in {MainModel.BaseYear}: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtBeginInitialCost):N2}
- Net change in {MainModel.CurrentYear}: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtBeginInitialCost):N2}
- Growing or shrinking? Accelerating or decelerating?

**3. Capital Investment Analysis**
- {MainModel.BaseYear} investment: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received:N2} thousand UAH
- {MainModel.CurrentYear} investment: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received:N2} thousand UAH
- Year-over-year change and %
- Investment as % of beginning balance (capital intensity)

**Investment Quality**:
- {MainModel.BaseYear}: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.ReceivedNewlyAcquired / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received * 100 : 0):N2}% were new
- {MainModel.CurrentYear}: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.ReceivedNewlyAcquired / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received * 100 : 0):N2}% were new
- Interpretation: 100% = modernization, <100% = used/transferred assets

**4. Asset Disposal Analysis**
- {MainModel.BaseYear} disposals: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left:N2}
- {MainModel.CurrentYear} disposals: {AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left:N2}
- Disposal trend

**Disposal Quality**:
- {MainModel.BaseYear}: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Liquidated / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left * 100 : 0):N2}% were liquidated
- {MainModel.CurrentYear}: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Liquidated / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left * 100 : 0):N2}% were liquidated
- Interpretation: High % = end-of-life disposals, Low % = assets still valuable

**5. Investment vs Disposal Balance**
- {MainModel.BaseYear} ratio: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Received / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.Left : 0):N2}x (Received/Left)
- {MainModel.CurrentYear} ratio: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left > 0 ? AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Received / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.Left : 0):N2}x
- Interpretation: >5x = aggressive expansion, 1-5x = growth with renewal, <1x = contraction

**6. Depreciation and Asset Age**
- {MainModel.BaseYear} depreciation rate: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost > 0 ? (AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation) / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Base.BalanceAtEndInitialCost * 100 : 0):N2}%
- {MainModel.CurrentYear} depreciation rate: {(AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost > 0 ? (AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost - AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndMinusDepreciation) / AvailabilityAndMovementOfFixedAssets.Current.BalanceAtEndInitialCost * 100 : 0):N2}%
- Trend: Increasing = aging, Decreasing = renewal
- Benchmark: 30-40% = new, 50-60% = mature, >70% = aging

**7. Strategic Pattern Recognition**
- Is company EXPANDING (net addition > 0)?
- Is company RENEWING (replacing old with new)?
- Is company CONTRACTING (net reduction)?
- What's the dominant strategy between years?

**8. Key Findings** (3-5 bullets)
- Most dramatic changes
- Investment quality assessment
- Disposal patterns
- Depreciation trends
- Strategic signals

**9. Strategic Recommendations**
**Capital Investment**:
- Optimal investment level for next year
- Focus areas for new acquisitions
- ROI expectations

**Asset Disposal**:
- Disposal optimization opportunities
- Asset lifecycle improvements
- Liquidation pattern concerns

**Depreciation Management**:
- Renewal urgency based on depreciation rate
- Target depreciation rate
- Modernization priorities

**Timeline**:
- Immediate (30 days): Urgent actions
- Short-term (3-6 months): Priority improvements
- Long-term (1-2 years): Strategic positioning

INTERPRETATION GUIDE:
? POSITIVE SIGNS:
- Received > Left = Growth
- High % new assets = Quality investment
- Low % liquidated = Assets retain value
- Decreasing depreciation rate = Renewal working
- Investment ratio >2x = Strong expansion

? CONCERNING SIGNS:
- Received < Left = Shrinking
- Low % new = Acquiring old assets
- High % liquidated = End-of-life crisis
- Depreciation rate >70% = Urgent renewal needed
- Investment ratio <1x = Underinvestment

EXAMPLE NARRATIVE:
""The company dramatically accelerated capital investment in {MainModel.CurrentYear}, spending 6.3 million UAH on new fixed assetsâ€”more than 2.5 times the 2.5 million invested in {MainModel.BaseYear}. Importantly, 100% of these acquisitions were brand new assets, demonstrating a commitment to modernization. This aggressive investment, combined with minimal disposals, resulted in net asset growth of 5.4 million UAH, expanding the asset base by 19%. The depreciation rate improved from 4.1% to 12.2%, reflecting the infusion of new equipment though the overall asset base remains relatively new.""

WRITING STYLE:
- Professional and analytical
- Active voice
- Integrate numbers with interpretation
- Explain WHY changes matter for business strategy
- Distinguish between expansion, renewal, and maintenance
- Provide actionable capital allocation insights
- Concise but thorough

Remember: Write in {languageInstruction}. NO tables. Focus on FIXED ASSET STRATEGY and what it reveals about capital investment decisions, asset renewal, and long-term capacity planning.";
    }

        }
